{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0233","billNumberShort":"S.B. 233","billNumberLong":"SB0233S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0563","shortTitle":"Judicial Performance Evaluation Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"BRAMMB","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Brammer, Brady","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"LISONK","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Lisonbee, Karianne","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill makes changes related to the Judicial Performance Evaluation Commission.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>amends definitions;<hr><ltbullet>renumbers and reorganizes statutory provisions in Title 78A, Chapter 12, Judicial Performance Evaluation Commission;<hr><ltbullet>addresses the requirements for a meeting of the Judicial Performance Evaluation Commission (Commission);<hr><ltbullet>requires the Commission to perform a study regarding reversal on appeal and provide a report to the Judiciary Interim Committee on the study;<hr><ltbullet>requires the Commission to allow a judge to appear and speak at a commission meeting in certain circumstances;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the requirements for the judicial performance survey, including the contents of the survey;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the certification standards for judicial performance, including the certification standards for a justice of the Utah Supreme Court and a judge of the Utah Court of Appeals; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Jacqueline Carlton","fiscalAnalyst":"Steven M. Allred","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/23/2026","trackingID":"MAURRXCDSJ","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-02 10:40:46.723","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"